TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Failed the gate spec-lint for a reason outside this task's authorized paths: the gate's own argv invokes cargo with the task worktree as its working directory, and cargo aborts with \"error: could not find `Cargo.toml` in /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/96facee9fb96/container-recipe or any parent directory\". The gate is defined in silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json as `bash -euc \"nix develop /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix --command cargo run -q -p spec-lint -- specs/flashnext --worklist silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json --root . || [ $? -eq 1 ]\"`. `nix develop <path>` enters that flake's dev shell but does not chdir into it, so `cargo run -p spec-lint` performs manifest discovery from the worktree. The estate repository is Python/bash/nix and contains no Cargo.toml and no .rs files anywhere (verified by find over the worktree); the linter crate lives at /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix/crates/spec-lint with package name spec-lint, and /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix/Cargo.toml exists. This is deterministic, not a machinery or session fault: every task worktree run of this gate fails identically before spec-lint executes, which is consistent with the stderr showing a cargo discovery error rather than any lint finding. The defect is also unrelated to this task's content — the second-attempt work is sound. repo-tests passed (witnessSeq 7028), the working tree is clean with no stray .build/ tree (attempt 1's ownership defect is fixed by moving CCACHE_DIR_HOST/PIP_CACHE_HOST to ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/flashnext), every committed path is inside container/ and results/receipts/, and the acceptance criterion recipe-pins re-runs green in the worktree (bash -n clean; torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0, repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch, mecattaf/vllm, flashnext:dev, and the MIT notice all present). No edit confined to container/ or results/receipts/ can make the spec-lint gate pass, because the failure is in the gate command's cargo manifest resolution, and silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json is outside the binding write boundary. The fix is to anchor cargo to the tally.nix manifest while leaving the working directory (and therefore the relative arguments specs/flashnext, --worklist silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json, --root .) resolving against the task worktree, by adding --manifest-path /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix/Cargo.toml to the cargo run invocation; cargo runs the built binary with the invoking cwd inherited, so the linter still sees the estate tree. The preflight test -d /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix already passes and needs no change, and the campaign's red line against mutating /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix is respected because only the worklist gate argv changes.","proposal":{"kind":"gate-set-fix","paths":["silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json"],"goal":"Make the spec-lint gate runnable from a task worktree that has no Cargo.toml by anchoring the cargo invocation to the tally.nix manifest, without changing which tree spec-lint lints and without mutating /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix. In silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json, replace the spec-lint gate argv with: bash -euc \"nix develop /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix --command cargo run -q --manifest-path /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix/Cargo.toml -p spec-lint -- specs/flashnext --worklist silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json --root . || [ $? -eq 1 ]\". Leave the preflightArgv, the gate id, and every other gate unchanged. The relative arguments continue to resolve against the gate's working directory (the task worktree), which is the intended lint target; only cargo's manifest discovery is redirected. After the amendment, re-run the container-recipe task's gate set; the committed container/ and results/receipts/ work needs no further change.","acceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"spec-lint-gate-manifest-anchored","description":"The spec-lint gate in the worklist anchors cargo to the tally.nix manifest and still lints the estate worktree with the same arguments.","argv":["bash","-euc","python3 -c \"import json,sys; g=[x for x in json.load(open('silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json'))['campaign']['gates'] if x['id']=='spec-lint'][0]; c=' '.join(g['argv']); assert '--manifest-path /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix/Cargo.toml' in c, c; assert '-p spec-lint' in c, c; assert '--worklist silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json' in c, c; assert '--root .' in c, c; print('ok')\""]},{"id":"spec-lint-runs-without-local-cargo-manifest","description":"Executing the amended spec-lint gate command from a directory tree that contains no Cargo.toml no longer aborts in cargo manifest discovery and produces no 'could not find Cargo.toml' error.","argv":["bash","-euc","test ! -e Cargo.toml; err=$(nix develop /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix --command cargo run -q --manifest-path /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix/Cargo.toml -p spec-lint -- specs/flashnext --worklist silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json --root . 2>&1 >/dev/null) || true; printf '%s\\n' \"$err\"; ! printf '%s' \"$err\" | grep -q 'could not find .Cargo.toml.'"]},{"id":"spec-lint-gate-green-in-worktree","description":"The amended gate command, run verbatim from the estate worktree, exits successfully under the gate's own exit-1 tolerance.","argv":["bash","-euc","nix develop /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix --command cargo run -q --manifest-path /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix/Cargo.toml -p spec-lint -- specs/flashnext --worklist silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json --root . || [ $? -eq 1 ]"]},{"id":"other-gates-unchanged","description":"The worklist still parses and the other four gate ids and their argv are untouched.","argv":["bash","-euc","python3 -c \"import json; gs=json.load(open('silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json'))['campaign']['gates']; ids=[g['id'] for g in gs]; assert ids==['repo-tests','spec-lint','flake-eval','fork-verify','receipts-verify'], ids; d={g['id']:g['argv'] for g in gs}; assert d['repo-tests']==['python3','-m','unittest','discover','-s','tests']; assert d['flake-eval']==['nix','flake','check','--no-build']; assert d['fork-verify']==['bash','scripts/verify-fork.sh']; assert d['receipts-verify']==['python3','scripts/receipts-verify.py']; print('ok')\""]}],"dependencies":[]}}
